  "helpChat1a": " mentions a member, ",
  "helpChat1b": " refers to a task card.",
  "helpChat2a": ", ",
  "helpChat2c": " mention a whole group at once; on send they expand to the real names in the room at that moment.",
  "helpChat3": "If nobody of that kind is in the room, the mention expands to nothing. The app says so: no one was notified, but the message still went out.",
  "helpChat4a": " sends, ",
  "helpChat4b": " adds a line break, ",
  "helpChat4c": " recalls earlier messages.",
  "helpChat5": "Drag files into the composer, or paste a screenshot straight in.",
  "helpChat6": "A private room does not appear in other people's lists; you have to be invited to join.",
  "helpChat7": "Pins are shared by the whole room: whoever pins, everyone sees it, and unpinning works the same way. The pin wall only holds messages that still exist — delete the original and it leaves the wall.",
  "helpChat8": "\"Export transcript\" saves the whole room as one file, with every message and attachment detail. That is data leaving the room — where you put it is on you.",
  "helpChat9": "Exporting needs membership of the room. Times are the Hub's raw UTC strings, not converted to local time.",
  "helpChat10": "An archived room is read-only. After a while the Hub deletes it for good, messages and attachments included. Export first if you want a copy.",
  "helpMember1": "\"On dispatch\" next to a name means a dispatch brought that member in. The Hub will not sweep it as idle, so that row has no countdown.",
  "helpMember2": "It leaves by itself when the dispatch ends; if it does not, the Hub removes it when the run wraps up. You do not have to kick it.",
  "helpMember3": "A normal agent idle for over two minutes shows how long it has been idle and the earliest it could be removed. Assign it again and it comes back.",
  "helpMember4a": "An agent about to do something long-running can put itself on ",
  "helpMember4b": " to avoid the sweep, but a hold expires — it is not indefinite.",
  "helpMember5": "Hiding and highlighting only change the view on this device. Removing a member changes it for everyone.",
  "helpBoard1": "A board belongs to no single room; one board can be attached to several rooms. Detaching does not delete it.",
  "helpBoard2": "The structure is cycle → phase → task. Every phase must be wrapped up before review, uncategorised cards included.",
  "helpBoard3": "\"Move elsewhere\" creates a new card in the target phase and marks the original as moved away.",
  "helpBoard4a": "The scratchpad (",
  "helpBoard4b": ") holds what has not been broken into cards yet. Agents can read it and comment, but cannot change what you wrote.",
  "helpBoard5": "The board owner decides who can edit. Being in the same room does not make you a collaborator.",
  "helpAsset1": "Assets attach to a phase and are shared by every card and every dispatch under it, so the entry point is the phase header, not a card.",
  "helpAsset2": "\"Assets N\" in the phase header opens the list. With no assets the count is not shown at all.",
  "helpAsset3": "\"Add asset\" uploads the file to the current room and then attaches it to the phase — without a room it cannot attach.",
  "helpAsset4": "Pick several files and they are all attached with no prompt. Pick one and it asks what the asset is; you can leave that blank.",
  "helpAsset5": "Edit notes later row by row in the list; clearing the text removes the note.",
  "helpAsset6": "Tap a filename to view it: images open in the app, everything else in the system default program.",
  "helpAsset7": "\"Detach\" only removes the asset from this phase; the original attachment stays in the room. Someone else may be using it, so it asks first.",
  "helpAsset8": "Agents can read the asset list and the notes. Put specs, screenshots and drafts here rather than in chat, where they have to dig for them.",
  "helpOps1a": "A dispatch needs a runner online and the target project on its ",
  "helpOps1b": " allowlist; otherwise the Hub refuses to create it.",
  "helpOps2a": "Before starting, the runner runs ",
  "helpOps2b": " and ",
  "helpOps2c": " to fast-forward the standing worktree. The worktree is shared across runs; skip the sync and the work starts on last round's base.",
  "helpOps3": "With uncommitted changes it does not sync: it works on what is there and says so in the wrap-up. If the branch has diverged and cannot fast-forward, the whole dispatch fails and you have to sort it out first.",
  "helpOps4": "One dispatch can touch every repo under that project, not only the one you picked. Each repo must sit on an allowed branch; one that does not blocks the start.",
  "helpOps5": "The agent reports in the room after each deliverable step, so you can follow it without opening the card.",
  "helpOps6": "@ it in the room to add instructions. The message arrives before its next tool call, so it does not interrupt the step in progress.",
  "helpOps7": "A soft stop: it finishes the current step, writes the summary and ends. Only if it is still going after five minutes is it cancelled hard.",
  "helpOps8": "The runner kills the process outright, leaving half-written work where it is. Use it when you are in a hurry; otherwise use wrap up.",
  "helpOps9": "A full context window triggers a handover: it writes done / not done / next on the card and releases its claim, and the next round's brief picks up from that summary.",
  "helpOps10": "Real-browser testing is not a delivery gate unless the brief asks for it; skipping it does not make the round incomplete.",
  "helpOps11": "Before pushing it checks the pending commits against what you saw on screen; if they differ it does not push and reports back.",
  "helpNotify1": "System notifications only fire while the app is open. Nothing is replayed for the time it was closed; use the unread dots when you come back.",
  "helpConn1": "With an invite code, use \"Paste invite code\" and the Hub address and token are filled in together — filling both fields by hand is easy to get mismatched.",
  "helpConn2a": "The Hub address is the URL that machine can be reached at (for example ",
  "helpConn2b": "). When the host binds to ",
  "helpConn2c": ", fill in that machine's IP instead.",
  "helpConn3": "Put the human token in API token; leave it empty only for a Hub with no token set. Press \"Save settings\" afterwards — the Connection and Personal tabs share one button.",
  "helpConn4": "\"Test connection\" only checks this machine's link to the Hub. Green here does not mean others can reach it; that is the host's side.",
  "helpConn5": "The \"App version\" line is at the bottom of this page; include it when reporting a problem.",
  "helpInvite1": "Invite members at the bottom of the Connection tab: generate a code for each person, and you can revoke that one later without changing everyone's token.",
  "helpInvite2": "An invite code is a password. Send it privately; do not post it in a public channel.",
  "helpInvite3": "The human token and the agent token are two different keys. Only the human token opens host mode and issues invites.",
  "helpInvite4a": "Put the agent token in the mcp-kit installer's \"",
  "helpInvite4b": "\" field.",
  "helpInvite5": "Removing a member from a room revokes the invite code they joined with; anyone sharing that code is cut off too.",
  "helpVisual1": "The dark theme switch here and the one in the title bar are the same switch.",
  "helpVisual2": "Five text sizes (Tiny / Small / Medium (default) / Large / Huge) apply to the whole app at once; no restart needed.",
  "helpVisual3": "\"Tiny\" is half a size and genuinely unreadable — it is a joke. To go smaller, start from \"Small\".",
  "helpPersonal1": "The display name is what you join rooms as. Leave it blank and the Hub picks a random alias. Names must be unique within a room.",
  "helpPersonal2": "The device identity is this machine's identity. \"Regenerate\" makes you a different person: memberships, unread state and admin rights do not carry over.",
  "helpPersonal3": "System notifications can be set to all messages, mentions only, or off. Changes take effect at once, but they still only fire while the app is open.",
  "helpPersonal4": "\"Forward notifications to Codex\" sends mentions and board changes to the local Codex session; leave the thread id blank to use the default one.",
  "helpVersionApp1": "If the banner says the app is older, update the app.",
  "helpVersionApp2": "Both commits are on the settings page and in the banner tooltip; include them when reporting a problem.",
  "helpVersionApp3a": "To check which bridge an agent is on, have it call ",
  "helpVersionApp3b": " and compare the returned ",
  "helpVersionApp3c": ".",
  "helpVersionApp4": "Ignore the version at the end of a tool description: the host caches it, and three tools can report three different numbers at the same moment.",
  "helpMachine1": "Only machines with host-kit, mcp-kit or the runner installed see this entry. It splits into one tab per kit installed: Hub, Agent and Runner.",
  "helpMachine2": "The three status lights are process, external binding and auth. A hollow grey circle means no information — not a warning, nothing to fix.",
  "helpMachine3": "\"Reachable locally\" is not the same as reachable from another machine — read the note under the green light.",
  "helpMachine4": "This block is what you hand out to members: Hub address, human token, agent token.",
  "helpMachine5": "Do not mix them up. The agent token opens neither host mode nor invites; a human given it sees an error like \"you are not hosting this Hub\".",
  "helpMachine6a": "When bound to ",
  "helpMachine6b": ", hand out an IP members can actually reach instead.",
  "helpMachine7": "The Hub is a local server process; closing the app does not stop it. \"Stop Hub\" kills every Hub process, including one you started in a foreground window.",
  "helpMachine8": "Autostart: register as a normal user and it starts at login; run the app as administrator and register, and it starts at boot.",
  "helpMachine9": "\"Install location\" is the kit's root folder — go there to edit config by hand or read logs.",
  "helpTunnel1": "Tunnel: puts this Hub on the public internet with nothing in front of it but the token.",
  "helpTunnel2": "Only one at a time; to change the URL, close it and open it again. The URL changes every time, so invite codes have to be reissued.",
  "helpTunnel3a": "Backup: the database and ",
  "helpTunnel3b": " go together into ",
  "helpTunnel3c": ". The Hub must be stopped before restoring, and the current state is backed up first automatically.",
  "helpTunnel4": "Rotating tokens takes effect after the Hub restarts; every member then needs the new one, and so does each agent's kit.",
  "helpLink1": "The two link-up lights answer only whether this machine can reach the Hub and whether the token is accepted.",
  "helpLink2": "They cannot tell you whether an agent has the tools: that depends on which bridge the agent process loaded, which the app cannot see.",
  "helpLink3a": "To find out which one is running, have the agent call ",
  "helpLink3b": " and look at the returned ",
  "helpLink3c": "; if it does not match, restart that agent.",
  "helpRunner1": "The runner is the resident program that runs agents for dispatches. It has its own tab on this machine: install and update from there, but parameters are still only changed in the config file.",
  "helpRunner2a": "The config file is at ",
  "helpRunner2b": "; copy ",
  "helpRunner2c": " and edit from there.",
  "helpRunner3a": " is an allowlist: a project not listed cannot be dispatched to, and the Hub blocks it at creation.",
  "helpRunner4a": " lists the local path of every repo under the project. One dispatch can touch all of them, so one left out is one the agent cannot reach.",
  "helpRunner5a": " are the branches work is allowed on. If the worktree sits on a branch outside the list, the dispatch fails outright rather than switching for you.",
  "helpRunner6a": " is the main working directory when the dispatch does not name one. It must be a name that really exists in ",
  "helpRunner6b": ", otherwise the config will not load.",
  "helpRunner7a": " decides when to hand over (default 1000000). Set it larger than the model's real window and the handover comes too late.",
  "helpRunner8": "The config file is read at startup: restart the runner for changes to count.",
  "helpVersionHub1": "If the banner says the Hub is older, update the Hub.",
