  "helpGroupInstall": "Install and update",
  "helpChatStyleLead": "Speaking style",
  "helpChatStyle": "The top-bar menu sets how agents talk in this room: verbose, concise, casual, or a custom instruction. Only room admins can change it.",
  "helpBoardSupLead": "Supervisor",
  "helpBoardSup1": "Each room can name one supervisor; a room admin presses Assign. A temporary member brought in by a dispatch cannot be one.",
  "helpBoardSupDispatchLead": "A supervisor can dispatch",
  "helpBoardSup2": "An agent acting as supervisor can dispatch on this board itself: investigate, implement a ticket, finish a phase. Only humans can push.",
  "helpBoardSupQuotaLead": "Quota and triggers",
  "helpBoardSup3": "What it dispatches counts against the quota of the human who named it, and nothing fires on its own: finishing a phase does not dispatch the next one for it.",
  "helpBoardDirectiveLead": "Rulings",
  "helpBoardDirective": "Rulings from the supervisor or the owner go into the audit trail. They can go to everyone or name one person, and everyone on the board sees them.",
  "helpBoardOwnerLead": "Handover and claim",
  "helpBoardOwner": "An owner can hand the board to someone else on it. Only a board with no owner can be claimed.",
  "helpOpsStartLead": "Starting a dispatch",
  "helpOpsStart": "Pick a template, pick the target project, write a brief. The brief is capped at 2000 characters.",
  "helpOpsTemplatesLead": "Three templates",
  "helpOpsTemplates": "Investigate reads only and changes no files; implement a ticket commits to an allowed branch but does not push; finish a phase lets the agent break it into cards and work through them.",
  "helpOpsPushLead": "Pushing",
  "helpOpsPush": "Pushing is not a template: the dashboard button builds that dispatch, and only a human in the room can press it — an agent cannot dispatch one.",
  "helpOpsDashboardLead": "Where the dashboard is",
  "helpOpsDashboard": "The dispatch dashboard lives in the ops room: unpushed commits, the last few hours of usage, running and queued dispatches, and runner state are all there.",
  "helpOpsLead2": "Syncing the worktree",
  "helpOpsLead3": "When it cannot sync",
  "helpOpsLead7": "Wrap up",
  "helpOpsLead8": "Cancel",
  "helpOpsLead9": "Handover",
  "helpNotifyExcLead": "Dispatch exceptions",
  "helpNotifyExc1": "The bell in the top bar collects dispatch exceptions across rooms: stalls and recoveries, timeouts, rate limits, runners going offline and back.",
  "helpNotifyExc2": "The unread count only covers entries newer than the last time you looked; tapping one jumps to the room it happened in.",
  "helpMachineLead4": "Connection info",
  "helpMachineLead5": "Two tokens",
  "helpInstallLead": "Installing from a release",
  "helpInstall1": "Every tab has an \"Install and update\" block: it fetches the matching version from a GitHub release, downloads it, unpacks it and runs the installer.",
  "helpInstallReleaseLead": "Only the matching release",
  "helpInstall2": "A version with no matching release cannot be installed this way; use the installer package instead.",
  "helpInstallBlockedLead": "When the button is disabled",
  "helpInstall3": "Four reasons: already on the release version, this version has no release, no Python 3.12 found, or the runner still has runs in hand (drain it from the dashboard first).",
  "helpInstallHubLead": "Updating the Hub",
  "helpInstall4": "The Hub is stopped before it is reinstalled, and you start it again yourself afterwards. Windows may ask for permission along the way.",
  "helpInstallConfigLead": "Config files",
  "helpInstall5": "An existing config file is not overwritten; the installer says so when it finishes.",
  "helpEnvLead": "Editing .env",
  "helpEnv1": "The Hub and Agent tabs edit that kit's .env directly: Hub changes need a restart, MCP changes take effect on the next connection.",
